      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for inpatients of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the higher dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you really do want the original dose, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
